.TH WERKMEISTER-FEATURE-STATUS 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-feature\-status \- Show all features, services, resource usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister feature status\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Show individual container details
.TP
\fB\-\-intercepts\fR
Show Telepresence intercept state only (per feature service; cheap — skips docker and k8s probes).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output structured JSON (useful for agent\-driven diagnosis)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows shared infrastructure, every active feature and the k8s port\-forwards in one view.
.PP
\fBOutput example:\fR
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
=== Werkmeister Status ===

  Infrastructure
  Service                    Status
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  caddy                      healthy
  k8s\-forwards               healthy
  mcp\-web\-server             healthy

  Features
  Host load 1.8 2.1 2.0 (10 cores)  |  feature containers 14% CPU
  Slot  Feature                    Services                             Ports            Status
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     1  my\-feature                 backend, frontend                    11100\-11119      up (2/2)  12.3% CPU · 410 MiB · started 2 h ago by up
     3  other\-feature              frontend                             11300\-11319      partial (0/1)

  k8s Port\-Forwards
  Service                    Ports              Health check                  Status
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  redis                      :9050 → :6379      (tcp)                         alive
  postgres                   :9051 → :5432      (tcp)                         alive
  backend                    :9052 → :80        /health                       alive
  frontend                   :9053 → :8080      /                             dead

  2 active feature(s), 10 slot(s) available  |  k8s: 3/4 alive

  To restart dead forwards: docker restart w9r\-k8s\-forwards
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBStatus indicators:\fR
.IP \(bu 3
\fBup (N/M)\fR (green) — all containers running
.IP \(bu 3
\fBpartial (N/M)\fR (yellow) — some containers running
.IP \(bu 3
\fBpaused (0/M)\fR (cyan) — every container paused
.IP \(bu 3
\fBdown (0/M)\fR (red) — no containers running
.IP \(bu 3
\fBno containers\fR (dim) — compose file exists but no containers found
.PP
A feature's row ends with its CPU and memory and how long ago it started, when known. A container that keeps restarting adds a red \fB✗ <service> crash\-looping (N restarts)\fR line under it; \fB\-\-verbose\fR lists each container. Features waiting for a slot show as \fBWaiting for capacity: <feature> (#1)\fR.
.PP
\fB`werkmeister infra status`\fR shows only the k8s port\-forwards (\fBfeature status \-\-k8s\fR is deprecated). Each forward is one row: the listen port on this machine mapped to the remote port, the health check (\fB(tcp)\fR or an HTTP path) and \fBalive\fR, \fBdead\fR or \fBunknown\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
=== k8s Port\-Forward Status ===

  k8s Port\-Forwards
  Service                    Ports              Health check                  Status
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  redis                      :9050 → :6379      (tcp)                         alive
  postgres                   :9051 → :5432      (tcp)                         alive
  backend                    :9052 → :80        /health                       alive
  frontend                   :9053 → :8080      /                             dead

  3/4 services alive

  To restart dead forwards: docker restart w9r\-k8s\-forwards
.RE
.fi
.PP
When the forwards container is not running, it says so instead of listing rows: \fBnot running\fR (start it with \fBwerkmeister infra connect\fR), \fBcontainer w9r\-k8s\-forwards is down\fR, or \fBstopped — not needed by any running workspace\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
